\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Blocking and what survives it}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{A field averaged over larger blocks has fewer observable coordinates.
For the [hierarchical Gaussian families](fdip-0098), this averaging
returns another hierarchical precision. Which parameters of the finer
field can still be recovered from the coarser Gaussian probability law?}

\p{The [blocking step and its towers](fdip-01CF) start with orthogonal
projection of a positive Gaussian precision and classify the families
compatible with repeated rescaled averaging. [Scaling directions](fdip-01CO)
compare precision and polynomial-observable families under these steps.
The pairings are the counting inner products, and the scalar fields are real.}

\p{The [limits of repeated blocking](fdip-01D1) compare arbitrary
hierarchical profiles with finite-range grid couplings. On a periodic
grid with fixed coordinates and field amplitude, the latter limits
determine the mass parameter and second-moment tensor.
[Blocking an interaction](fdip-01DC) gives the exact single-site
integral, its second-order quartic term, and the decrease along a
finite flow under explicit bounds on its input potentials.}

\transclude{fdip-01CF}
